From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:16:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] chore(art): drop the availability table, its generators,
 and its plumbing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The unconditional rewrite made all of this dead weight: with nothing choosing a
printing, there is nothing to look up, so the measured per-printing availability
table no longer has a reader.

Removed:

  * scripts/gen-derived-art-availability.sh and its two Python helpers
    (probe-derived, fetch-index-art) — ~500 lines of probing/index-fetching for a
    file nobody reads
  * the `__SCRYFALL_IMAGES_AVAILABILITY_URL_TEMPLATE__` define from
    vite.config.ts, vitest.config.ts and vite-env.d.ts
  * the 1.5 MB generated sidecar itself (gitignored build output)

That is the concrete benefit of the rewrite: the fork no longer maintains a
per-printing table for any locale, and a fresh build no longer spends ~6 minutes
producing one. The README keeps a short section recording what the removed design
was and why it could not be made consistent — the failure is worth remembering,
since "measure first, then choose" looks obviously correct until two callers
choose differently.
